## Changed sections

**`src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc`** — new *The holder* section after `restart`; judge and vocabulary untouched. Namespace docstring amended: the holder no longer "joins when built", plus a holder paragraph (no ledger, no clock, renewal advances a bound only on `:dao.stream/ok`, bound bounds attention not access).

- `initial-holder` — threaded plain-map state; validates `:self`, `:grantor`, `:resolver` (fn?), interval shape, unit table at assembly. Same refusal logic as `initial-judge`'s R1 resolver check: a holder with no working attribution would falsely never renew.
- `renewal-interval` `[units duration proposed]` — H2 as amended: throws unless `interval + interval < duration` (exactly S1's relation), so equality-at-half throws; cross-unit via the shared table.
- `observe-grant` `[holder source fact reading]` — H1: holds the grant only when it is structurally valid `:accepted`, names `:self`, and the composition's `(resolver source fact)` seam attributes it to `:grantor`. Anything else returns the holder unchanged (`:grant` nil = "no grant observed"). Keep-first basis; `reading` is the holder's own tick reading.
- `observe-renewal` `[holder reading outcome]` — advances the basis only on `:dao.stream/ok`.
- `due-to-renew?` `[holder reading]` — H2: fires when elapsed has *reached* the interval (equality included, vs the judge's strict `exceeds?`); false before any grant and after `stop`.
- `at-bound?` `[holder reading]` — H3: reached (≥) the earlier of duration-since-later-of(last renewal, grant) and cap-since-grant.
- `stop` `[holder]` — H4: returns `{:holder …stopped… :release (release lease-id)}`; throws with no grant observed. No `:lapsed` path and no reclaim exists in the section (structural).

Naming note: §4.3's "`release` (H4)" is the Phase-1 fact constructor the holder authors; the new holder-side discipline function is `stop`, since `release` is taken in the namespace.

